      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #43540.\n\n`scripts/convert_otel_2_perfetto.py` rejects two supported trace inputs:\n\n1. A JSON array with insignificant leading whitespace is misdetected as JSONL. The format sniff only inspects the very first character, so a compact array is parsed as JSONL and later crashes with `TypeError: list indices must be integers or slices, not str`, while a pretty-printed array crashes with `JSONDecodeError` on the first line.\n2. A normal OTLP span from `service.name=smg` crashes with `KeyError: 'child'`. `build_otel_span_tree` initializes the internal `child` field for engine spans only, but the shared perfetto converters (`__convert_to_perfetto_span`, `__convert_to_perfetto_events`) also expect it on SMG spans.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `load_otel_data`: detect the input format from the first *non-whitespace* character (`content.lstrip().startswith(\"[\")`), so a whitespace-prefixed JSON array is no longer mistaken for JSONL. The JSONL path is unchanged.\n- `main`: initialize the internal `child` field (`span.setdefault(\"child\", [])`) for SMG spans after tree building, so an OTLP exporter never has to provide the converter's internal field. `setdefault` keeps any exporter-provided value intact.\n- Removed four provably unused imports (`collections.defaultdict`, `typing.Iterable/List/Tuple`) that were already flagged by `ruff check --select F401` before this change.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Ran the exact reproduction from the issue (stdlib only): plain array, space-prefixed compact array, and newline-prefixed pretty-printed array of an SMG span. Before: all three exited 1 (`KeyError: 'child'`, `TypeError`, `JSONDecodeError` respectively). After: all three exit 0 and produce byte-identical Perfetto output containing the complete SMG span.\n- Regression: a JSONL input and a mixed engine+SMG input convert unchanged; the JSONL and whitespace-prefixed-array forms of the same trace produce identical output.\n- Audit: `ruff check --select F401,F821,F823,UP037` and `ruff format --check` pass on the file, `python3 -m py_compile` passes, `git diff --check` is clean, no added line exceeds 88 cols. No existing tests reference this script.\n- Honest caveat: this machine has no GPU and the converter needs none (standard library only), so verification was limited to the CLI-level reproduction above; CI is needed for any broader integration signal.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #38142682945](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38142682945)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38142682857](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38142682857)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
